---
// The load-bearing chart: two mean per-task cost deltas with bootstrap CIs, on
// one axis, with the A/A control's interval drawn as a shaded band across the
// whole plot so you can see the treatment's mean land inside the noise.
// Delta is off minus on, so positive means headroom was cheaper.
import { responsive } from './plot.js';
import { costDelta as d, money3, dollarTick } from './data.js';
import * as Plot from '@observablehq/plot';

const label =
  "The treatment's mean cost saving of $0.367 per task sits inside the A/A control's own 95% confidence interval, and both intervals straddle zero.";

const hue = (a) => (a.role === 'control' ? 'var(--chart-grey)' : 'var(--accent)');

const { wide, narrow } = responsive(
  (width) => ({
    width,
    height: 214,
    marginTop: 24,
    marginBottom: 48,
    marginLeft: 16,
    marginRight: 16,
    x: { domain: d.domain, ticks: d.ticks, tickFormat: dollarTick, label: null },
    y: { domain: d.arms.map((a) => a.label), axis: null, label: null, padding: 0.5 },
    marks: [
      // the A/A control's own interval, drawn as context rather than a series
      Plot.rectX([{ x1: d.band[0], x2: d.band[1] }], {
        x1: 'x1', x2: 'x2', fill: 'var(--chart-band)',
      }),
      Plot.ruleX(d.band, { stroke: 'var(--rule)', strokeWidth: 1 }),
      Plot.ruleX([0], { stroke: 'var(--dim)', strokeWidth: 1 }),

      Plot.ruleY(d.arms, {
        y: 'label', x1: (a) => a.ci[0], x2: (a) => a.ci[1],
        stroke: hue, strokeWidth: 2,
      }),
      Plot.tickX(d.arms, { y: 'label', x: (a) => a.ci[0], stroke: hue, strokeWidth: 1.5, insetTop: 12, insetBottom: 12 }),
      Plot.tickX(d.arms, { y: 'label', x: (a) => a.ci[1], stroke: hue, strokeWidth: 1.5, insetTop: 12, insetBottom: 12 }),
      Plot.tickX(d.arms, { y: 'label', x: 'median', stroke: hue, strokeWidth: 3, insetTop: 8, insetBottom: 8 }),
      Plot.dot(d.arms, {
        y: 'label', x: 'mean', r: 5,
        fill: hue, stroke: 'var(--bg)', strokeWidth: 2,
      }),
      Plot.text(d.arms, {
        y: 'label', text: 'label',
        frameAnchor: 'left', textAnchor: 'start', dy: -18,
        fill: 'var(--dim)', fontSize: 12,
      }),
      Plot.text(d.arms, {
        y: 'label', x: 'mean', text: (a) => money3(a.mean),
        dy: -18, fill: 'var(--ink)', fontSize: 12,
      }),
      Plot.text(d.arms, {
        y: 'label', x: 'median', text: (a) => `median ${money3(a.median)}`,
        dy: 24, fill: 'var(--muted)', fontSize: 11,
      }),
      Plot.text(['pricier with headroom'], {
        frameAnchor: 'bottom-left', textAnchor: 'start', dy: 36,
        fill: 'var(--muted)', fontSize: 11,
      }),
      Plot.text(['cheaper with headroom'], {
        frameAnchor: 'bottom-right', textAnchor: 'end', dy: 36,
        fill: 'var(--muted)', fontSize: 11,
      }),
    ],
  }),
  label
);
---

<figure class="fig">
  <p class="fig-head">mean per-task cost delta, off minus on</p>
  <p class="fig-sub">dot is the mean, bar is the median, line is the 95% bootstrap CI</p>
  <div class="fig-key">
    <span><i class="sw sw-band"></i> A/A control noise band</span>
    <span><i class="sw sw-dot sw-grey"></i> on-cache, control</span>
    <span><i class="sw sw-dot sw-accent"></i> on-token, treatment</span>
  </div>
  <div class="plot-wide" set:html={wide} />
  <div class="plot-narrow" set:html={narrow} />
  <div class="fig-stats">
    {d.arms.map((a) => (
      <div>
        <b>{a.label}, {a.role === 'control' ? 'A/A control' : 'treatment'}</b> n <i>{a.n}</i>
        &middot; Wilcoxon p <i>{a.p}</i> &middot; Cohen's dz <i>{a.dz}</i> &middot;
        <i>{a.cheaper}</i> cheaper / <i>{a.pricier}</i> pricier
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    Running the identical configuration twice, which is what the control arm is, already produces an
    apparent saving of <b>$0.730</b> per task. The treatment's <b>$0.367</b> lands inside that band, its
    median is <b>negative</b>, and more of its tasks came out pricier than cheaper. There is no effect
    here to measure.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
